        <review>&lt;p&gt;Leaner and more suspenseful than many of Dickens's sprawling serials, &lt;em&gt;A Tale of Two Cities&lt;/em&gt; builds steadily from a foggy Dover mail-coach mystery into a deeply felt story of loyalty and redemption.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Both its opening lines and its final chapter are deservedly among the most famous in English prose.&lt;/p&gt;</review>
